  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Hii Mission Technologies recorded $1.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company won 84 awards with an average award size of $12.7M, and obligations are down 7.9% year over year. The General Services Administration is the largest buyer, accounting for $873M of obligations, followed by the Department of Defense with $195M. Other buying agencies include the Department of the Interior with $443K and the Department of Education with $388K. Engineering Services and All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services are the two biggest NAICS markets, with $496M and $534M in obligations, respectively. Smaller markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $30.7M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $5.3M. FY2026 to date sits alongside prior annual totals of $596M in FY21, $657M in FY22, $595M in FY23, $1.1B in FY24, and $1.2B in FY25. This profile shows concentration in civilian procurement through GSA and a mix of engineering and professional services work.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "Who are Hii Mission Technologies' main federal buyers?",
        "body": "The General Services Administration is the main buyer, obligating $873M in FY2026 to date. The Department of Defense is the second-largest buyer with $195M. The Department of the Interior and the Department of Education are much smaller buyers with $443K and $388K respectively. Other agencies include the Department of Homeland Security with $18.8K and the Department of Commerce with $4K."
      },
      {
        "heading": "What markets and services drive Hii Mission Technologies' federal obligations?",
        "body": "All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services and Engineering Services drive the largest shares, with $534M and $496M respectively. Other significant markets include Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing at $30.7M and Other Support Activities for Air Transportation at $12.2M. R&D in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounts for $5.3M and Software Publishers accounts for $657K."
      }
    ]
  },
  "faq": [
    {
      "q": "How much does Hii Mission Technologies make from federal contracts?",
      "a": "Hii Mission Technologies has $1.1B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The company received 84 awards so far this fiscal year with an average award size of $12.7M, and obligations are down 7.9% year over year."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies buy from Hii Mission Technologies?",
      "a": "The General Services Administration and the Department of Defense are the primary buyers. The General Services Administration obligated $873M and the Department of Defense obligated $195M in FY2026 to date, with much smaller obligations from the Department of the Interior ($443K) and the Department of Education ($388K)."
    },
    {
      "q": "What does Hii Mission Technologies sell to the government?",
      "a": "Hii Mission Technologies sells professional, technical, and engineering services and some aerospace and R&D work to the government. All Other Professional, Scientific, and Technical Services and Engineering Services account for $534M and $496M respectively, while Other Aircraft Parts and Auxiliary Equipment Manufacturing accounts for $30.7M and R&D in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounts for $5.3M."
    },
